  "details": "**### Description**\n\nThere is an intermittent issue with the avatar change button in the main menu. Sometimes, clicking the button does not result in the avatar being changed with a single click. However, the avatar sometimes changes successfully after multiple clicks or occasionally on the first try. This issue is not isolated to my account alone; I have shared this problem with several friends, and at least ten of them have confirmed experiencing the same behaviour.\n\n**### Steps to Reproduce**\n\n1. Navigate to the main menu.\n\n2. Click on the avatar change button.\n\n3. Observe whether the avatar updates on the first click.\n\n**### Expected vs. Actual Behaviour**\n\n Expected Behaviour:\n\n- Clicking the avatar change button should consistently update the avatar with a single click.\n\n Actual Behaviour:\n\n- The avatar sometimes does not change upon the first click.\n\n- Multiple clicks may be required to successfully change the avatar.\n\n- Occasionally, the avatar changes with a single click.\n\n**### Environment**\n\n- Verified on both JP and USW instances.\n\n- No known causes identified.\n\n**### Impact**\n\nThis issue affects the user experience by making avatar changes unreliable and potentially time-consuming. Since multiple users are affected, addressing this problem would improve usability for a significant portion of the community.\n\n**### Additional Information**\n\nThe problem persists across different instances (JP and USW), suggesting it is not region-specific. No recent changes or updates have been identified that could be causing this behaviour.\n\n**### Request**\n\nPlease investigate the underlying cause of the intermittent failure of the avatar change functionality in the main menu and implement a fix to ensure that avatars can be changed reliably with a single click.\n\nThank you for your attention to this matter.",
